# AI Layer Rules

## Prompts Live in One Place
All prompt strings must be defined in `lib/ai/prompts.ts` (or `lib/ai/prompts/` as a folder with one file per prompt type once the single file exceeds 300 lines). Never write prompt strings inline in API routes or components.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — prompt hardcoded in route
const response = await anthropic.messages.create({
  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: `Write a LinkedIn post about ${topic}` }]
})

// ✅ GOOD — prompt from prompts.ts
import { prompts } from '@/lib/ai/prompts'
const response = await anthropic.messages.create({
  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: prompts.generateSocialPost(brandContext, platform, brief) }]
})
```

## Server Only
AI calls happen in API routes only (`app/api/`). Never call Anthropic or OpenAI from a Client Component. API keys must never be exposed to the browser.

## Brand Context Always Injected
Every generation prompt must include `brand_context` from the database. Never generate content without it.

## Model is a Variable
The model name (`claude-3-5-haiku-...`, `claude-sonnet-...`) is a constant in `lib/ai/generate.ts`, not scattered across files. Changing the model means changing one line.
